    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "doc: fix msg argument description of nonce function typedefs",
    "user": {
      "login": "amartya1523",
      "id": 133855728,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOB_p58A",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133855728?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/amartya1523",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The docs for `secp256k1_nonce_function` and `secp256k1_nonce_function_hardened` both describe the message argument as the one \"being verified\". Nonce functions are only ever called from the signing functions, so the first commit changes this to \"being signed\".\n\nThe hardened nonce function docs also say `msg` is NULL if and only if `msglen` is 0. That is stricter than what `secp256k1_schnorrsig_sign_custom` enforces: it only checks `msg != NULL || msglen == 0` and passes `msg` through to the nonce function unchanged, so a custom nonce function can see a non-NULL `msg` with `msglen == 0`. The second commit uses the same \"Can only be NULL if msglen is 0\" wording that `sign_custom` already has.",
    "labels": [],
