      "message": "doc: msg passed to hardened nonce function can be non-NULL when empty\n\nThe hardened nonce function docs claimed msg is NULL if and only if\nmsglen is 0. secp256k1_schnorrsig_sign_custom only requires that msg is\nnon-NULL when msglen is non-zero and hands msg through to the nonce\nfunction unchanged, so a caller signing an empty message may pass either\nNULL or a non-NULL pointer. Use the same wording as sign_custom.",
